samsung has been on a roll lately  putting out four sets of wireless  earbuds  in less than two years each one with  significant improvements compared to the  last  including these new galaxy buds pro if  you buy them  most of you will be really happy so why  is it that i'm having a hard time  recommending them  after using them extensively every day  for a week now  and what are the two problems that i've  personally experienced  with them that's exactly what you'll  find out after watching this review  as well as which earbuds i would  recommend instead of these and why  which are also linked down in the video  description below let's start out with  the good  and the first thing that really stands  out is the sound quality  samsung is once again using dual drivers  like in the galaxy buds plus  but they've redesigned them and you  could definitely hear the difference  listening to them side by side they  promised balanced sound  and wide frequency response with rich  bass silky treble  and a wide sound stage now i would agree  to almost  all of that the dual drivers definitely  provide deep rich bass and that treble  stands out  particularly in songs with a lot going  on such as rock music where these  provide  great instrument separation and clear  vocals the only  thing that i wouldn't agree to is their  claim of a wide soundstage  now it's not bad but it's nothing  special and samsung's own  galaxy buds lives are noticeably better  if you care about this  these things sound fantastic for earbuds  and after using these for a bit it is  tough to go back to my earpods pro  because of the lower sound quality the  difference is very noticeable  with that if you're an iphone or a mac  user i had no problems using these  they paired without any issue and they  connected consistently and quickly  pretty much right away every time i  pulled them out of their charging case  of course you won't get all of the  features on an iphone such as 360 degree  sound  which is similar to apple's spatial  audio or the ability to read out  messages and having a hands-free  assistant  but if you don't care about these things  they worked great  and they also had great range and the  sound quality was indistinguishable  compared to when i had them connected to  my galaxy note 20. now samsung  still hasn't updated their galaxy buds  app for ios  but thankfully these earbuds sound the  best in their default normal mode  so no need to go into the app in order  to change the eq like you had to do with  the galaxy buds plus for the gamers out  there these have about 300 milliseconds  of latency which isn't great  and it's right there right at the line  of being usable  depending on the game and how picky you  are but it is a good improvement  compared to the previous versions  and surprisingly the performance is the  same on the iphone  even though you don't have that gaming  toggle what really stands out is  watching videos and especially movies on  these  where of course there is no latency  because of the improved dual drivers  the rich deep bass is much closer to a  real surround sound system than most  earbuds  and all of those really low sounds that  shake you in an action scene  are actually immersive and they pull you  into the film and with that the vocals  are still  very clear and easy to understand  instead of being muffled by the action  apple please use dual drivers and your  airpods pro 2.  it will take your excellent spatial  audio to the next  level and with that apple please copy  their voice detect feature this is one  of my favorite new features which allow  you to keep active noise cancellation  enabled  and when you start talking they will  automatically go into the ambient mode  and stay there until you don't talk for  about 10 seconds  in real world use this usually worked  really well and 10 seconds was enough  of a buffer for most conversations it  does take about 2 seconds for them to  switch from the time you start talking  and i did have a few times where they  would switch back too early  so it would be nice to be able to adjust  this to say maybe 30 seconds  but this feature is definitely not a  gimmick with that the ambient mode  actually sounds pretty good being a big  improvement compared to the buds plus  and the default normal mode sounds the  most natural  i think a big part of this is because of  the much better microphones  take a listen for yourself to how the  mic compares to the galaxy buds plus  and my earpods pro this is the  microphone quality of the galaxy buds  plus  this is a microphone quality that you  can expect with samsung's new  galaxy buds pro and this is the  microphone quality with apple's airpods  pro  in real world use i didn't have a single  phone call where the person on the  opposite side  had a hard time hearing me even when i  was in loud environments  and each time i asked how i sounded they  responded that my voice was clear and  easy to hear  great job samsung that is a big  improvement another strong point  is battery life now sure they can't  touch the crazy 11 hours or so  with the galaxy buds plus but i don't  expect any earbuds with active noise  cancellation to last  that long and samsung's claims of about  5 hours with anc on  is spot on and the buzz charge really  quickly  when you put them into their charging  case together you get a total of up to  28 hours of use  but that claim is based on use without  active noise cancellation  with it on it's more like about 18 hours  which is still very good  and i only had to charge twice in the  last week simply by placing the case on  a wireless charging pad for a few hours  while using the buds and then they are  good to go speaking of the charging case  samsung ditched the older longer style  and they're using a square case like the  galaxy buds live came with  but with a few updates the earbuds are  easier to place in  and both of the magnets that hold the  buds and the ones that hold the lid  are quite a bit stronger personally i  miss the older shape since it took up  less width in my pocket  which is really nice especially if you  have a wallet in that pocket but for  most people it won't matter and the case  is fairly small compared to many other  brands  one of the ways that the pros stand out  compared to samsung's older earbuds and  most that are on the market  are their waterproofing rating these are  rated ipx7 which means that they can be  fully submerged  in over three feet of water for 30  minutes and they should still work  that is way better than the previous  ones which are rated mostly for splashes  but even though they have this rating  samsung still doesn't recommend using  them  on the beach or in pools and if they get  damaged it doesn't seem like samsung  will replace them  still having this rating gives way more  confidence  that they will hold up great when  working out or if you're using them  outside  say in the rain or the snow so that was  a lot of talk about the good things that  the new pros offer  but what are the two problems that i  talked about and  why is it hard for me to recommend these  the first issue i found when using them  is long-term comfort when i first tried  them on they were surprisingly  comfortable because samsung redesigned  the silicon tips so they are much  thicker and with that it's mostly just  the tips that go into your ears  just like the airpods pro and also with  that they added an  air vent to release pressure build up  similar once again to the airpods pro  these definitely improved the in-ear  comfort but that's not where i had an  issue the actual buds themselves  increased in size quite a bit  filling in the space in your ear so that  they can fit all the new tech in there  while not having them stick out of your  ear any more than before  because of this after about an hour and  a half my ear starts hurting where the  buds pro  touch and after about two hours i have  to take a break from using them  and i'm not typically someone who has an  issue with earbud fit  regular earpods were great for me as do  the pros  the sony's and the same thing with the  galaxy buds live so it's a bummer that  these aren't working out  and i can't use them as long as i can  with other earbuds  now this might not be an issue for you  but since they are  quite big if you have smaller ears i  would definitely keep this in mind  my next problem is the active noise  cancellation  it does work and it works better than  the galaxy buds live which are only  useful in select environments  which led me to call their ink more of a  marketing tool than an actual useful  feature  my issue is that it doesn't work well  enough for earbuds that cost  200 and it's only slightly better than  the galaxy buds plus  which have no cancellation whatsoever  and they block out a ton of noise  simply because they have a sealed design  without an air vent the airpods pro  noise cancellation is  noticeably better and the sonys are even  better than that  because of this if you're looking at the  galaxy buds pro for their noise  cancellation  i wouldn't count on it being great and  if that's the main reason for buying  them  over the galaxy buds plus i wouldn't do  it with that the main reason why i can't  recommend these  is because of how good the galaxy buds  plus are  and because of the price where you can  currently get them for 109  brand new and under 80 refurbished  which is a shockingly good price for  those i'll go ahead and leave links down  in the video description to those deals  now sure the galaxy bud pros do sound  better and they have a better microphone  but is it worth paying double for those  improvements and then having slightly  less noise  in some environments honestly no  i don't think so and with that if you  want comfort and even better sound  quality than the galaxy buds pro  and you don't need to block out noise  check out the galaxy buzz live  which are now 140 bucks or possibly even  less when you're watching this video  i'll go ahead and link those down below  as well overall the galaxy buds pro  are great earbuds and i have very little  complaints if they fit your ears  and dropping 200 for them doesn't hurt  your wallet  you will really enjoy them but seeing  how fast samsung is releasing new ones  i bet will soon have some that are more  comfortable and have  way better active noise cancellation go  ahead and click over there if you guys  want to see my full  detailed comparisons and click above to  subscribe to see more videos like this  one and help us reach 600k subs before  our official two year mark that would be  awesome thank you guys for watching and  i'll see you in the next video

